{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1340553-combat-rules","id":1340553,"title":"Combat Rules","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-09T22:34:14-07:00","id":1340553,"title":"Combat Rules","content":"Hi everyone. I and my friends are about to start a Changeling 2e campaign, and as I was creating my character I realized that defense rating is much too powerful.<br /> <br /> My friend made a character with 2 STR and 2 brawl. My character has a defense of 4, because of 2 DEX and 2 athletics. <br /> Now, my character doesn't have brawl at all, so in combat, we have no hope to hit each other. (His dice pool is reduced to 1 {hit only with 10} because of my defence, and the same goes for my character).<br /> <br /> So unless you have a really big dice pool, you won't really hit anything, and even with a big dice pool, it will most likely be reduced to something like 4-5 dice. <br /> <br /> I am not sure that defense should have been connected to the athletics skill. I mean, a trained MMA fighter should destroy an Olympic long-distance runner in combat. But according to the rules, the DEX + Athletics of the long-distance runner will most likely reduce the MMA fighter's dice pool to 1 or 2.<br /> <br /> So to my question. Have I understood the rules correctly? and, do you have issues with this in your games?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24461-godforsaken","name":"Godforsaken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24461_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-09T22:53:39-07:00","id":1340559,"title":"","content":"This is what Willpower and all-out attacks are for, as well as leveraging surprise, uneven numbers, and weapons.<br /> <br /> Also, 4-5 dice is not a small pool \u2014 it's literally the standard size for an average Attribute and professional-baseline Skill without extra equipment.<br /> <br /> (Also-also, Skill dots are not the only means by which characters qualify as the things that they are \u2014 note that in 2e there's a core Merit that literally makes it so that you can get a Specialty worth two dice for the same cost in Experiences as one dot in a Skill.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-09T23:00:22-07:00","id":1340561,"title":"","content":"The two relevant bullet points, if you're trying to seriously hurt or kill somebody:<ul><li>Spend Willpower. <i>Always</i> spend Willpower. Spend every point of Willpower you've got. Willpower is to be spent when something matters to you and is worth pushing yourself for, and a serious fight is always important enough to be worth that. +3 dice is a good deal. 3 dice will roll a success on the average.</li> <li>Pick up a weapon. Buy a nine millimeter. Pick up a pole of rebar. Break windows. If you're using the Beaten Down rules and not fighting to the death you only need one lucky blow to pretty much get your way. In a fight to the death, non-lethal damage is a handicap.</li> </ul>If you're <i>not</i> seriously trying to hurt or kill somebody, then you shouldn't be using the Violence rules. What kind of fight are you in that your character has zero training in any relevant fighting Skill and you're not trying to run away? It's not really that unusual that a guy who's average aside from knowing how to fight competantly, and a guy who's average aside from knowing how to stay away from a fighter competantly, neither of whom are pushing themselves or straining by spending Willpower, aren't really bowling each other over with their bare hands.<br /> <br /> I waver now and then on how I feel about Athletics adding to Defense, but these low-trait examples don't tend to bother me, no. If you're not trained in combat, your heroic efforts shouldn't involve getting into fights; getting into a serious fight means you already messed up. Your efforts should involve finding ways to get your way without having a dude try to crack your skull.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","user":"Stupid Loserman","date":". 10-10-2019, 02:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-09T23:11:30-07:00","id":1340565,"title":"","content":"A MMA fighter should at least have the Defensive Combat Merit for Brawl among many other things (Brawl replaces Athletics for Defense), on top of all sorts of other Merits to make them very hard to beat in combat.<br /> <br /> 2e is purposefully designed so that combat generally exists in the 0-4 dice range for two significant reasons:<br /> <br /> 1) It makes sure combat is more exciting. 1e combat had lower Defense, which just turned combat into an alpha-strike system where you would throw everything into attacking first, and attacking with 15+ dice (probably a few times with multiple-attack Merits) to one-shot people ASAP. Making it hard to get more than ~4 dice to attack means it's rare to reliably take down opponents in one or two hits.<br /> <br /> 2) The movement of Damage from adding to attacks rolls, to adding to damage dealt with the attack if it hits, means a single success can easily end a fight with bigger weapons (see: stun rules). Brawling is a bit of a slog, but weapons without significant defense turn combat insanely deadly extremely quickly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-10T00:07:20-07:00","id":1340570,"title":"","content":"Most of the relevant points have already been made, so I'm going to throw in what amounts to a nitpick.<br /> <br /> One of the problems of 1e, in my opinion, was that it defaulted to trying to do up an interesting combat simulator too much of the time, which is a fairly common problem IMO. 2e has done much better in that regard; the games aren't trying to model an accurate fighting simulator anymore. <b>They're trying to model a dramatic fight scene.</b> Athletics factors into Defense more because someone who's good at moving should feel harder to hit than because it meaningfully contributes to their ability to block a punch.<br /> <br /> So if you're using the Violence rules, <b>remember to start by stating Intent</b>. Why is the MMA fighter punching the long-distance runner? Is it to punctuate an argument they're making? Is it to build them up with a friendly tap? Is it to mock their lack of combat skill? All of those call for different possible Skills to come into play, and none of them really merit bringing out the full combat system.<br /> <br /> If you have a serious fight going on between an MMA fighter and the long-distance runner, then they should have a host of other things that are part of their character. As Heavy Arms notes, the fighter is going to have a small suite of relevant Merits. The runner should similarly have a lot more options than just sitting there and taking it. If the fighter takes a swing and misses, that should have a psychological effect. You just <i>whiffed</i> on some puny guy who doesn't know how to fight? Throw Willpower in, as Stupid Loserman says, and perform an All-Out Attack. Your Str 2, Brawl 0 attack against a Dex 2, Athletics 2 defense now yields 7-4=<b>3 dice</b>. That gives a pretty good shot at a success... and that's an extremely unrealistic MMA fighter, who'd never be caught without at least 3 Brawl dots.<br /> <br /> And remember: don't roll unless it makes sense to. Try to resolve it narratively before you go to the dice, and take a look at Down and Dirty Violence as an option when there's an obvious winner and loser, where you're <b>usually rolling the same Attr+Skill combo against each other</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-10T04:24:55-07:00","id":1340596,"title":"","content":"Well, that's up for my GM, but I see your point, and it looks quite logical and awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24461-godforsaken","name":"Godforsaken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24461_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T15:12:22-07:00","id":1341953,"title":"","content":"Also, use the Grappling rules. Most real world fights between people (that don't involve weapons) end up as a rolling around on the ground kind of hitting each other but mostly just tiring people out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}